      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and the extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** An overdose like this raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg per day,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order. If 1700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, tell me, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review first."
      }
     ],
